{
  "requirement": "During one call to `verify`, direct reads by the criterion and\nreads served by the SDK's agent tools record inputs in the same\n`ValidationContext`. For example, if criterion code reads a test and the agent\nthen reads its helper, both node fingerprints accompany the returned answer.\nA subsequent verification starts with an empty dependency list.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Structural obligations derived from `shared_context`:**\n1. During one `verify`, the criterion's direct reads and the reads served by agent tools record into the same `ValidationContext`.\n2. A later verification starts with an empty dependency list.\n\n**Obligation 1: one shared context**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#fn[verify]` builds one `ValidationContext` with `ValidationContext::new`. `fn[execute_with_context]` passes it as `&mut ctx` to `criterion.execute`. It then reads `ctx.dependencies()` into the returned `Fingerprinted`.\n- The criterion's direct reads (`read`, `read_snapshot`, `outgoing_edges`, `successors`) in `procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#2` record into that context's `observations` through `record_read` and `observe_edges`.\n- `procedure.rs#impl[Ask<...>]#2/fn[execute]` passes the criterion's own context to the agent with `agent.run(request, self.ctx)`. It does not create a separate context.\n- `agent/tools.rs#impl[ToolAgent<P, T>/Agent<D>]/fn[run]` receives that `&ValidationContext` as `inspection`. It stores the reference in `GraphSession.inspection` (`struct[GraphSession]`).\n- `GraphSession`'s `dispatch` collects dependencies from the agent tools into `pending`. The `read_node`, `outgoing_edges` and fallback source-tool branches all do this.\n- `converse` in `agent.rs` calls `session.delivered()` after each response. `GraphSession`'s `delivered` drains `pending` into the shared context with `record_read` and `observe_edges`.\n- Agent-tool reads and direct criterion reads therefore land in the same `observations` list, which is returned with the answer.\n\n**Obligation 2: empty start**\n- Each call to `verify` constructs a fresh context through `ValidationContext::new` and `configured`. `configured` sets `observations: Default::default()`, which is empty. The context is moved into `execute_with_context` and not reused, so a subsequent verification starts with an empty dependency list.\n- `agent.rs#fn[verify_with_agent]` follows the same pattern.\n\n**Gaps and scope**\n- I found no structural gap, ambiguity or unavailable information.\n- No acknowledgments (`{fixme}`) apply.\n- I did not assess the behavioral outcomes, such as the exact fingerprints returned in the worked example.\n- `references` shows no `{test}` edge to `shared_context`. Tests that exercise shared reads, such as `agent/tests.rs#fn[concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads]`, are marked against `ValidationContext`. The task asks for a structural assessment, so I did not treat this as a gap.",
  "references": "2c35862fa48dbc05e8825f322f614b0f35937ab779b0239d61752080a67691e4",
